# This project is written on Windows and runs on Linux, and git on the Windows side has
# core.autocrlf=true — so without these rules a fresh clone rewrites every file with CRLF.
#
# For source that is only ever read by a parser it makes no difference. For anything the kernel
# executes it is fatal and the error does not say so: `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` fails as
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M: no such file or directory", and a CRLF
# docker-entrypoint.sh puts the container into a restart loop that looks like a broken image.
#
# Pinning these to LF costs nothing on Windows — the editors here all handle LF — and removes a
# whole class of deploy failure.

*.sh            text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# The SQLite database is ignored, but say it plainly: line-ending translation on a binary file
# corrupts it, and that is not obvious from the extension.
*.db            binary
